WEBVTT

00:09.330 --> 00:10.750
I'll go.

00:11.250 --> 00:12.870
I'll go with you.

00:19.910 --> 00:21.290
Wait, Asuka?!

00:21.290 --> 00:22.750
What the hell?

00:23.540 --> 00:25.290
Sorry, senpais...

00:25.290 --> 00:28.830
Asuka, you don't need to sacrifice yourself.

00:29.290 --> 00:31.290
Sorry, guys!

00:31.290 --> 00:33.660
Oh, Yu, hold onto this for me.

00:45.870 --> 00:47.500
You are serious, then?

00:48.000 --> 00:49.000
Yup!

00:50.700 --> 00:52.080
Don't!

00:53.330 --> 00:54.750
Yu-senpai...

00:57.330 --> 00:58.410
Asuka...

00:59.290 --> 01:00.830
come back safe, okay?

01:02.160 --> 01:03.250
I will.

01:23.370 --> 01:26.750
Why'd you let her go, Yu-senpai?

01:27.000 --> 01:29.450
Yeah, that was kind of a big deal.

01:29.450 --> 01:33.160
No, I think Yu had an idea, right?

01:33.450 --> 01:36.500
It's not even really an idea.

01:36.950 --> 01:38.290
I just...

01:38.290 --> 01:41.910
I just know that Asuka intends to come back.

01:44.450 --> 01:47.290
I believe in Asuka.

01:51.290 --> 01:52.370
Hey...

01:52.950 --> 01:55.950
do you always walk along this way?

01:59.250 --> 02:02.330
C'mon, you invited me to come with you, right?

02:02.330 --> 02:04.950
Well, I'm here, so you can stop ignoring me!

02:04.950 --> 02:08.660
Eventually, you too will hear the voice of the Twilight.

02:08.660 --> 02:12.620
Then, there will be no need for us to exchange words.

02:12.620 --> 02:14.120
When's that going to happen?

02:14.120 --> 02:17.080
What day, what time, what minute, what second?

02:18.500 --> 02:19.950
Soon.

02:25.700 --> 02:27.330
I'm hungry.

02:27.620 --> 02:30.370
Time is stopped for us.

02:30.370 --> 02:32.410
You should not grow hungry.

02:32.410 --> 02:38.000
There's no way I wouldn't get hungry
after walking and talking!

02:38.620 --> 02:42.540
I got it! Let's go eat chikuwa
on some Fragment somewhere!

02:42.540 --> 02:43.750
No.

02:43.870 --> 02:46.580
I wanna eat chikuwa!

02:46.580 --> 02:49.080
Chikuwa! Chikuwa!

02:49.080 --> 02:51.700
Chicken wings! Chikuwa!

02:51.700 --> 02:54.700
Whoops, I said the wrong thing for a sec!

02:55.580 --> 02:57.040
A Little Bit of Deliciousness

02:57.200 --> 02:58.870
Aw, yeah!

02:59.080 --> 03:01.790
I'm so glad we found a Fragment
that uses our money!

03:01.790 --> 03:05.660
Oh... Maybe they look the same,
but they're counterfeits in this world!

03:05.660 --> 03:07.330
Am I a criminal now?

03:07.330 --> 03:09.290
Shut up and eat already.

03:12.000 --> 03:13.540
Here, have one.

03:15.200 --> 03:16.790
Give it a try!

03:16.790 --> 03:20.660
The crispy skin on this chikuwa
is so savory and delicious!

03:21.950 --> 03:23.660
C'mon!

03:23.660 --> 03:27.830
Chikuwa! Chikuwa!

03:27.830 --> 03:29.410
Chiku...

03:37.080 --> 03:39.870
You can tell me how good it is, y'know!

03:44.870 --> 03:47.910
Hey, you're me, right?

03:47.910 --> 03:49.950
So you like chikuwa too, yeah?

03:50.200 --> 03:53.750
I told you, I have abandoned all emotion.

03:55.040 --> 04:00.660
I just thought that you might have started liking
chikuwa in the same way I started liking chikuwa.

04:01.250 --> 04:04.370
For me, it was Kyo-chan.

04:08.750 --> 04:10.200
Nothing!

04:10.200 --> 04:13.870
Jeez, I asked mom to leave us some snacks!

04:13.870 --> 04:18.040
Maybe she had to go for a rush delivery, and she forgot.

04:18.040 --> 04:20.700
Ugh, I'm so hungry...

04:22.750 --> 04:23.950
What about this?

04:25.200 --> 04:27.410
A Little Bit of Deliciousness

04:25.200 --> 04:26.660
Ta-dah!

04:27.660 --> 04:30.000
Chikuwa? It's not even sweet.

04:30.000 --> 04:32.830
But you can use it to tell your fortune!

04:32.830 --> 04:34.250
What? How?

04:35.500 --> 04:40.250
Bite into a chikuwa, and the god of chikuwa
will answer any question!

04:43.660 --> 04:48.700
According to the god of chikuwa,
I'll get a perfect score on my test tomorrow!

04:48.700 --> 04:51.290
Really? Lemme try!

04:51.660 --> 04:52.660
Well?

04:53.700 --> 04:56.000
I'm gonna get a perfect score, too!

04:56.000 --> 04:58.370
Really? Yay!

05:01.410 --> 05:04.790
I didn't actually get a perfect score, though.

05:08.330 --> 05:10.000
72%...

05:10.410 --> 05:11.330
Huh?

05:21.410 --> 05:23.540
A message from Lord Chikuwa himself!

05:23.540 --> 05:27.790
He says that there might be
a Kyo-chan here on this fragment!

05:28.700 --> 05:30.450
Let's go find out!

05:36.500 --> 05:37.750
Oh...

05:37.750 --> 05:40.160
So this Kyo-chan's not here, either.

05:41.040 --> 05:44.450
I have visited many Fragments.

05:44.450 --> 05:48.870
No matter the world, he always
disappeared on that fateful day.

05:49.200 --> 05:53.040
Well, even if everyone so far was a bust,
maybe you'll find him on the next one.

05:53.040 --> 05:55.160
Such a thing is clearly impossible.

05:55.160 --> 05:57.040
No, it's not!

05:59.450 --> 06:02.500
Asuka-chan? Are you home?

06:03.160 --> 06:05.200
You're home early today.

06:05.200 --> 06:06.040
Oh?

06:07.290 --> 06:09.700
My old ears must be hearing things.

06:15.660 --> 06:17.950
Kyo-chan wasn't there.

06:19.330 --> 06:21.500
He exists nowhere.

06:21.500 --> 06:23.080
I told you this.

06:24.330 --> 06:25.750
Still...

06:25.750 --> 06:28.250
I can't give up on him.

06:28.540 --> 06:32.790
If Kyo-chan were in my shoes,
I know he wouldn't give up on me.

06:37.870 --> 06:41.000
I've had it! We're not gonna find it!

06:41.000 --> 06:44.790
But that's the keychain that matches Yu's, right?

06:44.790 --> 06:47.790
I'll just tell her I'm sorry. Let's go!

06:57.040 --> 06:59.200
He was like that.

06:59.870 --> 07:02.200
Oh, do you remember that, too?

07:04.330 --> 07:05.790
You know...

07:06.200 --> 07:10.830
Whenever something's giving me a hard time,
I think of Kyo-chan in that moment.

07:11.160 --> 07:15.000
It helps me find the energy to press on a little longer.

07:16.750 --> 07:18.080
That's it!

07:18.080 --> 07:21.080
Kyo-chan is still there, deep inside of me!

07:21.410 --> 07:22.950
I bet he's inside you, too.

07:22.950 --> 07:24.200
He is not.

07:24.910 --> 07:26.910
He is not inside of me.

07:27.250 --> 07:30.250
Ever since the day he disappeared,
he no longer exists.

07:31.750 --> 07:32.700
Still...

07:32.700 --> 07:34.290
You are a fool.

07:34.290 --> 07:38.200
You attempt to carry on, lying to your own heart.

07:38.200 --> 07:40.870
I do no such thing.

07:41.910 --> 07:43.410
Right.

07:44.540 --> 07:47.080
You don't lie, after all.

07:48.160 --> 07:51.080
But I was a liar.

07:52.080 --> 07:53.870
I'm sorry... I'm sorry...

07:52.450 --> 07:53.870
Back then, too...

07:53.870 --> 07:55.330
I'm sorry... I'm sorry...

07:55.870 --> 07:57.500
I'm sorry...

07:58.200 --> 08:00.370
You don't need to apologize, dear.

08:00.370 --> 08:04.540
Nobody thinks it was your fault.

08:04.790 --> 08:06.370
I'm sorry...

08:06.790 --> 08:08.290
I'm sorry...

08:08.580 --> 08:09.950
I'm sorry...

08:10.290 --> 08:14.290
When Kyo-chan disappeared, I cried a whole lot.

08:15.040 --> 08:18.750
But it wasn't because I was sad
about losing Kyo-chan.

08:19.910 --> 08:23.410
It was so the grown-ups wouldn't think it was my fault.

08:23.950 --> 08:26.620
I wanted them to pity me.

08:27.200 --> 08:29.330
That was the real reason.

08:30.580 --> 08:35.080
At first I did it subconsciously,
but one day, I figured out why.

08:35.950 --> 08:37.790
Was it the same for you?

08:39.790 --> 08:43.250
I started to hate myself for doing that.

08:43.950 --> 08:46.580
I thought I deserved to be punished somehow.

08:47.160 --> 08:49.370
Punished for losing sight of Kyo-chan.

08:50.040 --> 08:53.580
Punishment for crying for myself, and not for him.

08:53.580 --> 08:56.540
I know what I'm gonna do, Yu!
I'm gonna take over the family business!

08:57.040 --> 09:01.410
I was going to live the life
that Kyo-chan couldn't anymore.

09:01.950 --> 09:05.500
Even though I knew those very feelings were fake.

09:06.370 --> 09:09.330
You didn't choose to lie.

09:09.330 --> 09:11.620
You chose to abandon your emotions.

09:11.620 --> 09:13.830
But you did it for the same reason.

09:14.620 --> 09:16.500
You did it to punish yourself.

09:16.660 --> 09:18.500
That...

09:18.830 --> 09:20.870
You can't lie, right?

09:22.000 --> 09:25.500
That was the only thing I could do!

09:25.500 --> 09:27.910
There was nothing else I could...

09:29.910 --> 09:31.750
Asuka! I'm sorr-

09:44.120 --> 09:45.910
I won't...

09:47.040 --> 09:50.040
I won't talk to anyone about Kyo-chan ever again.

09:51.040 --> 09:52.910
I won't think about him ever again.

09:57.870 --> 10:01.200
I'll live as if he never existed in the first place.

10:16.540 --> 10:18.200
If that's how I'm living...

10:18.200 --> 10:21.370
then what does it matter if
everyone else never existed in the-

10:35.750 --> 10:38.450
The Twilight guided me.

10:38.450 --> 10:41.450
That day, I erased the world.

10:42.040 --> 10:44.080
I abandoned everything.

10:44.080 --> 10:45.700
I gave up.

10:48.750 --> 10:50.290
And yet!

10:50.580 --> 10:51.540
And yet!

10:51.660 --> 10:52.790
And yet!

10:53.000 --> 10:56.290
And yet!

10:57.040 --> 11:01.120
You made lots of friends, and smiled so much!

11:01.120 --> 11:02.620
It's not fair!

11:02.620 --> 11:04.250
Not fair, not fair, not fair!

11:04.250 --> 11:05.700
You should have nothing!

11:05.700 --> 11:07.910
You should lose everything, too!

11:12.290 --> 11:16.290
I've seen lots of Fragments, too.

11:16.830 --> 11:18.700
That's how I learned something.

11:18.700 --> 11:20.160
I learned...

11:22.830 --> 11:27.450
...that Asuka Tsuchimiya has
so many different possibilities.

11:28.410 --> 11:32.580
Despite that, I used my 'punishment' as an excuse
to squeeze my eyes shut to possibilities.

11:32.580 --> 11:35.410
Almost as if I were engulfed by the Twilight.

11:36.290 --> 11:41.700
That's why I won't use Kyo-chan as an excuse anymore.

11:42.500 --> 11:44.540
I won't blame anyone for it.

11:44.910 --> 11:46.950
Just as Yu said...

11:47.160 --> 11:49.750
just as Seriouska said...

11:51.040 --> 11:53.040
I have to face myself.

11:55.120 --> 11:59.330
The world is a result of the actions we take.

11:59.830 --> 12:04.040
Once you accept that fact, you can be free.

12:04.790 --> 12:08.500
I've decided to be free.

12:09.250 --> 12:13.040
It's okay for you to stop punishing yourself, too.

12:25.330 --> 12:27.950
But if I do that...

12:27.950 --> 12:31.580
then there won't be anyone left
who cares about Kyo-chan.

12:31.580 --> 12:33.540
You don't have to forget about him.

12:33.540 --> 12:37.290
Every now and then, you can remember him
and have a good cry.

12:37.290 --> 12:39.790
This time, you won't cry for yourself.

12:40.410 --> 12:43.500
You'll cry for Kyo-chan from the bottom of your heart.

12:44.700 --> 12:46.750
Is that really okay?

12:46.750 --> 12:49.580
Do you think Kyo-chan would forgive me?

12:55.750 --> 12:59.700
Kyohei Tsuchimiya, First Grade Class 3

12:56.000 --> 12:59.700
My name Kyohei means I'm living today in peace.

12:59.700 --> 13:04.160
Asuka Tsuchimiya, First Grade Class 2

13:00.160 --> 13:04.160
Your name Asuka means you're going to
walk across the bridge to tomorrow.

13:04.370 --> 13:08.580
Wait, that means I'm gonna
leave you behind, Kyo-chan!

13:09.040 --> 13:13.910
No, I'm always with you, Asuka-chan.

13:15.000 --> 13:18.750
After all, tomorrow will eventually be today.

13:19.370 --> 13:21.910
It's lying there just beyond the twilight.

13:22.120 --> 13:23.330
Always!

13:27.080 --> 13:28.750
It's okay.

13:28.950 --> 13:31.500
As long as tomorrow eventually becomes today.

13:32.750 --> 13:36.750
Kyo-chan will be with us.

13:38.870 --> 13:42.500
He's here with me too... right?

13:57.370 --> 13:58.700
Kyo-chan...

13:59.000 --> 14:00.660
Kyo-chan!

14:05.250 --> 14:06.620
Kyo-chan...

14:10.660 --> 14:12.660
This whole time...

14:30.580 --> 14:33.000
You've been with me.

14:36.580 --> 14:38.410
Goodbye, me!

14:39.040 --> 14:41.290
I hope I see you again someday.

14:42.540 --> 14:46.330
Beyond the twilight tomorrow...

14:48.160 --> 14:49.660
Asuka!

14:52.500 --> 14:53.410
Asuka!

14:53.410 --> 14:54.200
Asuka-senpai!

14:54.200 --> 14:55.000
Asuka!

14:55.000 --> 14:56.290
Asuka!

15:02.000 --> 15:05.790
I'm back, everyone!

15:08.000 --> 15:11.500
Miso

15:09.080 --> 15:11.500
Asuka! Hurry up!

15:11.950 --> 15:15.330
It's 7:30! You're going to be late, you know!

15:15.330 --> 15:17.870
Yeah, I know!

15:21.290 --> 15:22.790
There we go.

15:33.830 --> 15:38.160
You're a third year now, so you'd better start
giving yourself more time in the mornings!

15:38.160 --> 15:41.870
I don't need more time, I'm always calm!

15:44.120 --> 15:46.290
Huh? Asuka, are you for real?

15:46.660 --> 15:49.120
You want to go to the same college as Yu?

15:49.120 --> 15:51.200
That's a big change...

15:51.200 --> 15:52.410
You're crazy...

15:53.410 --> 15:55.160
Crazy courageous, I mean.

15:55.160 --> 15:57.080
Hey, c'mon, guys, you're so mean!

15:57.080 --> 16:01.330
The possibilities are infinite
for this here Asuka Tsuchimiya!

16:01.330 --> 16:05.950
I totally believe I can get my grades up
to where they need to be in a year!

16:06.290 --> 16:09.200
There's belief, then there's delusion.

16:09.580 --> 16:11.750
I'll be rooting for you.

16:12.500 --> 16:15.330
It'd be fun to go to the same college, anyway.

16:15.620 --> 16:16.830
Right?!

16:16.830 --> 16:19.330
I knew you'd say that, Yu!

16:19.330 --> 16:21.950
We could totally live in the same dorm room!

16:22.200 --> 16:24.950
Sounds good.
That'll help me save money on utilities.

16:24.950 --> 16:26.450
Is that all I'm good for?!

16:26.910 --> 16:28.620
Well, anyway.

16:30.080 --> 16:31.830
I'm gonna give it my all!

16:32.040 --> 16:35.410
For Yu, who believes in my potential!

16:39.200 --> 16:44.250
Oh, but still, maybe you should check out
the nearby university? It's a little easier to get into.

16:44.250 --> 16:47.700
You don't believe in my potential at all!
I can't believe you!

16:49.080 --> 16:52.000
Talking about all this makes you realize...

16:52.000 --> 16:56.000
This time next year, you guys won't be around anymore.

16:56.000 --> 16:58.870
That'll leave you in a tight spot.

16:58.870 --> 17:02.540
At this rate, I'm going to be the only person
left in the Radio Research Society!

17:02.540 --> 17:04.580
The club will be in serious trouble!

17:04.580 --> 17:06.790
We've just gotta get us some first years.

17:06.790 --> 17:10.870
Ones that are real easy to bully
into joining, like you, Mia!

17:10.870 --> 17:13.950
I wish it was harder for you to admit that...

17:16.290 --> 17:17.950
It's her!

17:20.410 --> 17:21.830
Hey, you!

17:22.120 --> 17:25.580
Uh, um...

17:26.040 --> 17:27.540
Mayuki-chan!

17:27.950 --> 17:29.080
Huh?

17:29.410 --> 17:32.120
Yes! It is you, Mayuki-chan!

17:32.120 --> 17:34.450
Oh, Seriouska's assistant!

17:34.450 --> 17:36.540
She ended up at our school!

17:36.540 --> 17:39.830
Wh-what is it? How do you know my name?

17:39.830 --> 17:42.540
A-and why are you calling me serious...?

17:42.540 --> 17:44.700
Oh, pay no mind to that!

17:44.700 --> 17:46.910
I'm Asuka Tsuchimiya.

17:47.160 --> 17:49.410
I know this is random, but...

17:49.950 --> 17:53.040
Do you wanna join the Radio Research Society?

17:57.500 --> 17:59.450
Oh, yeah, the Radio Society.

18:00.080 --> 18:01.330
Ha-wha...?

18:01.330 --> 18:03.290
What was that about just now?

18:03.290 --> 18:06.540
She practically spat the word from her mouth.

18:06.540 --> 18:09.080
I heard about you guys from one of
the senpais in the Broadcasting Club.

18:09.080 --> 18:13.450
She told me you guys were insane,
and to avoid you at all costs.

18:13.660 --> 18:16.200
Have you already joined the Broadcasting Club?

18:16.200 --> 18:19.370
Not yet, but I've already decided to join them.

18:19.370 --> 18:23.370
After all, my dream is to be a famous radio personality!

18:23.620 --> 18:27.750
My favorite radio host is Annie Maxda, after all!

18:28.040 --> 18:30.870
If that's the case, you might be better off
with the Radio Society...

18:30.870 --> 18:35.540
I hear the "Radio" part of your name's just for show,
and all you to is hang out at a café.

18:35.540 --> 18:38.250
I have no desire to be part of such a club.

18:38.250 --> 18:39.790
If you'll excuse me.

18:40.160 --> 18:41.790
Well, she's pleasant.

18:41.790 --> 18:44.870
She was so cute in that other world, too.

18:44.870 --> 18:46.450
You've left me no choice...

18:46.450 --> 18:49.450
I wanted to keep it a secret for a bit longer, but...

18:52.160 --> 18:55.290
Good afternoon, Akeyuki Academy
dudes and dudettes!

18:55.290 --> 18:58.200
DJ Asuka, from the Radio Research Society,
is now in da house!

18:58.200 --> 19:03.370
I'm here with a special guest to welcome
all y'all first years to our school!

19:03.620 --> 19:06.040
Hello, Akeyuki Academy!

19:06.250 --> 19:09.160
Good afternoon! This is Annie Maxda.

19:09.160 --> 19:13.250
I actually attended Akeyuki Academy back in the day!

19:09.160 --> 19:10.540
Annie?!

19:10.540 --> 19:13.250
Y-you're friends with Annie?!

19:13.250 --> 19:16.950
Oh, no, we just happened to
run into each other at Octave.

19:13.250 --> 19:15.660
And so, I'd like to dedicate a song

19:15.660 --> 19:17.870
to all my new underclassmen!

19:16.950 --> 19:20.160
She even called the owner there her "teacher".

19:17.870 --> 19:20.750
DJ Asuka-san, are you ready?

19:20.160 --> 19:21.370
She did?

19:20.750 --> 19:22.330
Hell yeah!

19:21.370 --> 19:22.330
Teacher?

19:22.330 --> 19:27.120
Okay, everybody, listen up, get up, start dancin'!

19:22.330 --> 19:24.120
Geez, who is he, really?

19:24.120 --> 19:26.750
Maybe he was a famous radio personality.

19:27.120 --> 19:30.410
F-Forget about that, I might be able
to meet Annie, right?!

19:30.410 --> 19:31.950
Take me with you, please!

19:31.950 --> 19:34.080
Aww, I dunno...

19:34.200 --> 19:35.450
I'll do anything!

19:35.450 --> 19:37.040
I'll be your friend forever!

19:37.040 --> 19:39.410
I'll join the Radio Society!

19:42.750 --> 19:44.000
Okay!

19:44.000 --> 19:46.620
Starting today, you're part of the Radio Society!

20:02.000 --> 20:09.080
Nanimo kikoenai nanimo kikasete kurenai

20:09.500 --> 20:17.080
Boku no karada ga mukashi yori otona ni natta kara nanoka

20:19.160 --> 20:27.000
Beddo ni oiteita hajimete katta kuroi radio

20:24.790 --> 20:27.000
Broadcasting Room

20:27.000 --> 20:34.660
Ikutsumo no melody ga ikutsumo no jidai o tsukutta

20:37.000 --> 20:43.500
Shishunki ni shounen kara otona ni kawaru

20:44.370 --> 20:51.660
Michi o sagashiteita kegare mo nai mama ni

20:52.200 --> 20:59.290
Kazarareta ikiba no nai oshiyoseru hitonami ni

20:59.830 --> 21:07.000
Hontou no shiawase oshiete yo kowarekake no radio

21:17.120 --> 21:22.160
I'd like to end today's broadcasts
with one of my favorite movie quotes.

21:22.700 --> 21:27.410
"Every morning, the world rises from their beds
to greet a new morning."

21:27.700 --> 21:32.080
"Yet you are still so afraid of what is new and unknown."

21:32.410 --> 21:37.700
Right then, let's not be afraid of the unknown,
and instead, charge forward towards it!

21:37.700 --> 21:39.290
You got it, Senpai!

21:53.120 --> 21:55.870
Huh? I'm up real early...

22:00.500 --> 22:02.370
Morning, Grandma.

22:02.370 --> 22:05.950
Asuka-chan! You're up early this morning.

22:05.950 --> 22:10.540
I woke up early for some reason,
so I thought I'd surprise my mom.

22:10.540 --> 22:11.790
Where is she?

22:11.790 --> 22:14.200
She's out handling a crisis!

22:14.200 --> 22:17.290
They came again, you see. The miso thief!

22:17.290 --> 22:18.290
Huh?

22:23.370 --> 22:25.660
Someone took some of it.

22:25.660 --> 22:27.750
A bento box full, it looks like.

22:27.750 --> 22:30.950
They must be a fan of our miso.

23:05.790 --> 23:08.410
The twilight sky I saw that day...

23:08.700 --> 23:11.290
shone with new light.

23:12.540 --> 23:15.500
There was nothing to fear.

23:16.120 --> 23:21.540
After all, our futures would always start today.

23:24.950 --> 23:29.870
Come forth, my twilight self!
